msgid "系统调用与 UAPI"
msgstr "System Calls and UAPI"

msgid "约定"
msgstr "Conventions"

msgid ""
"x86_64 使用 Linux syscall 编号与寄存器约定，未知接口返回 ENOSYS。 公开线协议位于 include/uapi，headers_install 由 "
"configs/header-export.list 控制；私有 task、页表和驱动状态不导出为用户 ABI。固定宽度、长度、版本、 边界和负 errno 都是接口契约的一部分。"
msgstr ""
"x86_64 uses Linux syscall numbers and register conventions; unknown interfaces return ENOSYS. "
"Public wire formats reside in include/uapi, and configs/header-export.list controls "
"headers_install. Private task, page-table, and driver state is not exported as a user ABI. Fixed "
"widths, lengths, versions, bounds, and negative errno values are all part of the interface "
"contract."

msgid "vDSO 的 ELF 符号版本、辅助向量、vvar 邻接映射及时间读取均有专用测试。 不支持的时钟或条件继续走真实 syscall，不返回猜测值。"
msgstr ""
"Dedicated tests cover vDSO ELF symbol versions, auxiliary vectors, adjacent vvar mappings, and "
"time reads. Unsupported clocks or conditions fall back to real syscalls rather than returning "
"guessed values."

msgid "兼容"
msgstr "Compatibility"

msgid ""
"公开头保留实际支持的兼容名称，旧用户库不能伪装成新 SONAME。 只实现的接口才可视为可用；头文件存在不能代替完整运行认证。 接口修改同步内核、导出头、用户态包装、消费者和必要验证，不以更新 "
"golden 替代布局或语义审查。"
msgstr ""
"Public headers retain compatibility names that are actually supported; old user libraries must not"
" masquerade as a new SONAME. Only implemented interfaces can be considered available; the presence"
" of a header does not establish full runtime certification. Interface changes must be synchronized"
" across the kernel, exported headers, userspace wrappers, consumers, and necessary validation. "
"Updating golden data does not replace layout or semantic review."

msgid "目录 bind mount"
msgstr "Directory Bind Mounts"

msgid ""
"``mount(source, target, NULL, MS_BIND, NULL)`` 支持非递归目录绑定。 新挂载保留源目录的实际 inode、父链和文件系统生命周期，继承源挂载的 "
"只读、nosuid、nodev 等策略。``/proc/self/mountinfo`` 的 root 字段报告源目录 在文件系统内的路径；命名空间路径、``..`` 和 chroot "
"边界按新挂载计算。 源文件系统在绑定仍存在时不能卸载，解绑不销毁源文件系统。 递归绑定、文件绑定和 bind remount 尚不支持，返回明确错误。"
msgstr ""
"``mount(source, target, NULL, MS_BIND, NULL)`` supports nonrecursive directory binds. The new "
"mount retains the source directory's actual inode, parent chain, and filesystem lifecycle, and "
"inherits source mount policies such as read-only, nosuid, and nodev. The root field of "
"``/proc/self/mountinfo`` reports the source directory's path within its filesystem; namespace "
"paths, ``..``, and chroot boundaries are computed relative to the new mount. The source filesystem"
" cannot be unmounted while the bind remains, and unbinding does not destroy it. Recursive binds, "
"file binds, and bind remounts are not yet supported and return explicit errors."
